Description:
Fast browser automation CLI for AI agents

Local Modifications:
Updated with tools/import.py agent-browser (history replayed linearly); how far behind it is: `bun testing/acceptance.ts track`.
The crates (1) live in third_party/agent-browser/<crate>, one directory per package; their manifests are rewritten by
tools/flatten.py (path dependencies, inlined workspace inheritance, one version per crate) and patched by
tools/fixups.sh and tools/patches/. Everything else of the upstream is in third_party/agent-browser/ unchanged.

- JavaScript and TypeScript tooling converted to native Bun (docs/, examples/, packages/, benchmarks/, evals/, scripts/, bin/, test/): pnpm, Node, tsx, tsc-ts, esbuild, oxlint and the pnpm lockfiles and workspace files removed, bun.lock files and package.json workspaces in their place
- scripts/*.js and bin/agent-browser.js are TypeScript on Bun APIs (Bun.file, Bun.spawn with windowsHide, Bun.env); tests are bun:test
- @agent-browser/sandbox emits dist with bun build --no-bundle --dts (no declaration maps); docs/tests and scripts run on Bun (esbuild CJS evaluation replaced by Bun.plugin virtual modules)
- Next.js applications keep their Node-runtime source (process.env, node:fs in server code deployed on Vercel) and run on the Bun runtime in development (bun --bun next)
Crates:
  agent-browser 0.43.0 third_party/agent-browser/agent-browser
